# Accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AA)

- Semantic HTML first (`button`, `label`, `nav`, `main`, `table`). ARIA only when semantics are insufficient.
- Text contrast ≥ **4.5:1**; large text and UI chrome ≥ **3:1** (1.4.3, 1.4.11).
- Do not convey meaning by color only (1.4.1): add text or icon.
- Visible focus (2.4.7). Focus order matches reading order. Modals trap and restore focus.
- Controls: name, role, value. Inputs have associated `<label>`. Errors in text, linked via `aria-describedby`.
- Target size ≥ 24×24px (2.5.8); **44×44px** on `/production/me` and shop-floor flows.
- Images: `alt` for product/measurement/QC photos; empty `alt` only if decorative.
- Motion: respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Do not auto-play video.
- Language: `lang="en"` on the document.
- Keyboard: all actions reachable without a pointer. Do not keyboard-trap except dialogs.

```tsx
// ❌
<div onClick={save}>Save</div>
<input placeholder="Phone" />

// ✅
<button type="submit">Save</button>
<label htmlFor="phone">Phone</label>
<input id="phone" type="tel" autoComplete="tel" />
```
